      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It has been shown that results of adenosine and dipyridamole myocardial scintigraphy are at least equivalent to those provided by conventional treadmill scintigraphy. Therefore, if a patient is unable to achieve a high rate-pressure product by treadmill exercise, that individual should be considered a candidate for pharmacological stress scintigraphy."},
